# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# setup: ideconnect
# board: discover
# Where a program goes is chosen in Connect, and the project remembers.
#
# Opening a project is when the shell looks for boards -- a deliberate
# act, and opening the machine's ports is worth it for a Connect menu
# that already lists what is here.  This desktop was never told to look.
# Picking a board there makes it the destination: Run reads as going
# there, and asking the shell to look again mounts nothing twice.
wait 60
click 980 30
wait 10
menu-pick Programming
wait 10
menu-pick TikuBasic
wait 250
expect-title Project
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick Open Project…
wait 40
expect-title Open
click 400 220
wait 6
click 675 413
wait 60
expect-no-title Open
click-window Project
wait 200
note runs go to this machine until a board is chosen
click 71 8
wait 8
expect-menu New Project…|Open Project…||Run||Close Project|
click-window Project
wait 10
note the boards the shell found when the project opened, and the one
note place a program can always go
click 175 8
wait 8
expect-menu This machine|tiku|tiku-2||Look again|
menu-pick tiku
wait 10
note and now Run says where it will go
click 71 8
wait 8
expect-menu Run on tiku|Save on tiku|
click-window Project
wait 10
note looking again finds the same boards, not the same boards twice
click 175 8
wait 8
menu-pick Look again
wait 400
click 175 8
wait 8
expect-menu This machine|tiku|tiku-2||Look again|
quit
